{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2092 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "d192c1308e79aa5d32a728deaa86822dd25c1b4dbfbd931454a268e5025b8235" :edb/db-before-t 2091 :edb/db-after-t 2092 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535404 50 #inst "2026-10-08T23:28:48.429Z" 13194139535404 true] [17592186087700 1020 #edb/ref 17592186347558 13194139535404 true] [17592186087700 1020 #edb/ref 17592186347572 13194139535404 true] [17592186087709 1020 #edb/ref 17592186347551 13194139535404 true] [17592186087709 1020 #edb/ref 17592186347565 13194139535404 true] [17592186087710 1020 #edb/ref 17592186347577 13194139535404 true] [17592186347551 1017 #edb/ref 17592186347552 13194139535404 true] [17592186347551 1089 "q-122726" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347551 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535404 true] [17592186347551 1100 "A curve is defined by the parametric equations \n\n$$\nx=4{t}^{5},\\,y=9t,\\,-\\infty <t<\\infty .\n$$\n\nDetermine the value of $t$ at which the tangent to the curve is vertical." 13194139535404 true] [17592186347551 1113 #uuid "5b4d0b60-e3bd-5983-83d6-629fbc513ac8" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347551 1145 "The slope $m$ of a tangent line to a curve defined parametrically is given by\n\n$$\nm=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nThe tangent line is vertical if ${x}^{′}(t)=0$ while ${y}^{′}(t)\\ne 0.$\n\nSo, we first find the derivatives of $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=20{t}^{4},\\,{y}^{′}(t)=9.\n$$\n\nSolving ${x}^{′}(t)=0$ gives\n\n$$\n20{t}^{4}=0\\,⟹\\,t=0.\n$$\n\nNote that ${y}^{′}(0)=9\\ne 0.$ Therefore, we conclude that when $t=0,$ the tangent to the curve is vertical." 13194139535404 true] [17592186347552 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347553 13194139535404 true] [17592186347552 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347554 13194139535404 true] [17592186347552 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347555 13194139535404 true] [17592186347552 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347556 13194139535404 true] [17592186347552 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347557 13194139535404 true] [17592186347552 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535404 true] [17592186347552 1041 "selection" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347552 1104 #edb/ref 17592186347553 13194139535404 true] [17592186347552 1110 #uuid "12c4a9ee-6329-5719-9169-2b8323892d0c" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347553 1034 "t=0" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347553 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535404 true] [17592186347553 1111 #uuid "9cefbaca-3550-55a0-b5a2-d5d79754501e" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347554 1034 "t=9" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347554 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535404 true] [17592186347554 1111 #uuid "8c6df50d-74eb-5d93-9081-e20be9a88127" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347555 1034 "t=20" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347555 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535404 true] [17592186347555 1111 #uuid "24228cd6-c60b-57dc-8824-c0513896faae" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347556 1034 "t=4" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347556 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535404 true] [17592186347556 1111 #uuid "7cf7e1e5-bcb8-5f04-bcc9-182d2b6580da" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347557 1034 "t=-1" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347557 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535404 true] [17592186347557 1111 #uuid "6bfd5ed9-6475-5ec2-91d2-17a5f57bce7d" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347558 1017 #edb/ref 17592186347559 13194139535404 true] [17592186347558 1089 "q-122931" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347558 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535404 true] [17592186347558 1100 "A curve is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx={e}^{t},\\,y=2t{e}^{t}-2{e}^{t},\\,-\\infty <t<\\infty .\n$$\n\nLet $C$ be the point that corresponds to $t=1$ on the curve. Find the equation of the normal to the curve at $C.$" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347558 1113 #uuid "138e1f42-3fb6-5013-87c6-eb59c3a912d0" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347558 1145 "First, we find the coordinates of the point $C$ by substituting $t=1$ into the parametric equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =e, \\\\ y & =2(1){e}^{1}-2{e}^{1}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we're looking to find the equation of the tangent line to the curve at the point $(e,0).$  For this, we need to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ which means we first need to find the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)={e}^{t},\\,{y}^{′}(t)=2t{e}^{t}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2t{e}^{t}}{{e}^{t}} \\\\  & =2t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=1,$ the slope of the tangent line is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={\\frac{dy}{dx}|}_{t=1} & =2(1)=2\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope ${m}_{n}$ of the normal line, we take the negative reciprocal of $m$:\n\n$$\n{m}_{n}=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{\\,2\\,}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the equation of the normal, we use point-slope form with the point $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(e,0)$ and the slope ${m}_{n}=-\\frac{1}{2}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-0 & =(-\\frac{1}{2})(x-e) \\\\ y & =-\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{e}{2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347559 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347560 13194139535404 true] [17592186347559 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347561 13194139535404 true] [17592186347559 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347562 13194139535404 true] [17592186347559 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347563 13194139535404 true] [17592186347559 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347564 13194139535404 true] [17592186347559 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535404 true] [17592186347559 1041 "selection" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347559 1104 #edb/ref 17592186347561 13194139535404 true] [17592186347559 1110 #uuid "3ed59925-3dd6-5551-ade5-4e6cbf1e3bc2" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347560 1034 "y=\\frac{x}{3}+\\frac{e}{4}" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347560 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535404 true] [17592186347560 1111 #uuid "02652485-045b-5d46-94a8-23202aa3e5f3" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347561 1034 "y=-\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{e}{2}" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347561 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535404 true] [17592186347561 1111 #uuid "783f33f1-7391-5ed6-8660-f05a8e52e776" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347562 1034 "y=-\\frac{x}{4}+\\frac{2e}{3}" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347562 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535404 true] [17592186347562 1111 #uuid "43cd01f5-06ff-57b6-8751-bb864623a753" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347563 1034 "y=\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{e}{4}" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347563 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535404 true] [17592186347563 1111 #uuid "1afebe6e-7606-5045-afe2-7d49c8b60693" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347564 1034 "y=\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{2}{e}" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347564 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535404 true] [17592186347564 1111 #uuid "0c2402b6-aacf-5739-8974-6606432ca65a" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347565 1017 #edb/ref 17592186347566 13194139535404 true] [17592186347565 1089 "q-21072" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347565 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535404 true] [17592186347565 1100 "A curve is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+5,\\,y=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+4,\\,0\\le t\\le \\pi .\n$$\n\nDetermine the values of $t$ at which the tangent to the curve is horizontal." 13194139535404 true] [17592186347565 1113 #uuid "62db0e45-63cb-50b4-b6ad-94c5afe9af6e" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347565 1145 "The slope $m$ of a tangent line to a curve defined parametrically is given by\n\n$$\nm=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nThe tangent line is horizontal if ${y}^{′}(t)=0$ while ${x}^{′}(t)\\ne 0.$\n\nSo, we first find the derivatives of $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nSolving ${y}^{′}(t)=0$ gives\n\n$$\n-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t=0\\,⟹\\,t=0,\\pi .\n$$\n\nNow, we note that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(0) & =3\\ne 0, \\\\ {x}^{′}(\\pi ) & =-3\\ne 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich confirms that the tangent to the curve is indeed horizontal when $t=0$ and $t=\\pi .$" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347566 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347567 13194139535404 true] [17592186347566 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347568 13194139535404 true] [17592186347566 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347569 13194139535404 true] [17592186347566 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347570 13194139535404 true] [17592186347566 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347571 13194139535404 true] [17592186347566 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535404 true] [17592186347566 1041 "selection" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347566 1104 #edb/ref 17592186347570 13194139535404 true] [17592186347566 1110 #uuid "d39a38dc-51bd-5b2b-80a3-191a3d1cbb23" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347567 1034 "$t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ and $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347567 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535404 true] [17592186347567 1111 #uuid "61bd84d2-4763-590b-be6a-188d4bf70820" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347568 1034 "$t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ and $t=\\pi $" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347568 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535404 true] [17592186347568 1111 #uuid "3bdc292d-2c36-5e29-8cb8-b1aa493c8278" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347569 1034 "$t=0$ and $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347569 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535404 true] [17592186347569 1111 #uuid "d7d2fbeb-09bc-56bd-91f7-79d97c674678" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347570 1034 "$t=0$ and $t=\\pi $" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347570 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535404 true] [17592186347570 1111 #uuid "7c7851e8-332f-58da-ae40-0cac35fae42d" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347571 1034 "$t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $t=\\pi $" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347571 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535404 true] [17592186347571 1111 #uuid "393d7715-24e4-5ca5-b2f2-9a08e2ece75b" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347572 1017 #edb/ref 17592186347573 13194139535404 true] [17592186347572 1017 #edb/ref 17592186347575 13194139535404 true] [17592186347572 1089 "q-350395" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347572 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535404 true] [17592186347572 1100 "A curve is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=7{t}^{2}-9t,\\,y={t}^{6}+2{t}^{2},\\,-\\infty <t<\\infty .\n$$\n\nLet $C$ be the point that corresponds to $t=1$ on the curve. Determine the coordinates of the point at which the normal to the curve at $C$ crosses the $y$-axis. Do not round the answers.\n\nThe normal to the curve at $C$ crosses the $y$-axis at $(${{field-1}},\n{{field-2}}$).$" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347572 1113 #uuid "7ce811e3-7f18-52e4-8f6f-84b575e03283" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347572 1145 "First, we find the coordinates of the point $C$ by substituting $t=1$ into the parametric equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =7({1}^{2})-9(1)=-2 \\\\ y & ={1}^{6}+2({1}^{2})=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we're looking to determine the equation of the normal at the point $(-2,3).$ For this, we need to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ which means we first need to find the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=14t-9,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=6{t}^{5}+4t\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)} \\\\  & =\\frac{6{t}^{5}+4t}{14t-9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=1,$ the slope of the tangent line is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={\\frac{dy}{dx}|}_{t\\,=\\,1} & =\\frac{6({1}^{5})+4(1)}{14(1)-9} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{5} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope ${m}_{n}$ of the normal line, we take the negative reciprocal of $m:$\n\n$$\n{m}_{n}=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the equation of the normal, we use point-slope form with the point $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(-2,3)$ and the slope ${m}_{n}=-\\frac{1}{2}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-3 & =-\\frac{1}{2}(x-(-2)) \\\\ y-3 & =-\\frac{1}{2}(x+2) \\\\ y-3 & =-\\frac{1}{2}x-1 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{2}x-1+3 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{2}x+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe normal crosses the $y$-axis when $x=0.$ At this point, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-\\frac{1}{2}(0)+2 \\\\ y & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the normal to the curve at $C$ crosses the $y$-axis at $(0,\\,2).$" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347573 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347574 13194139535404 true] [17592186347573 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535404 true] [17592186347573 1041 "field-1" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347573 1104 #edb/ref 17592186347574 13194139535404 true] [17592186347573 1110 #uuid "aae0949b-8861-50a2-8d79-737597369413" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347574 1034 "0" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347574 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535404 true] [17592186347574 1111 #uuid "7d6cc217-9664-5d4f-8cf0-e616bf47e6e4" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347575 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347576 13194139535404 true] [17592186347575 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535404 true] [17592186347575 1041 "field-2" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347575 1104 #edb/ref 17592186347576 13194139535404 true] [17592186347575 1110 #uuid "e4c3bb4b-951d-5aeb-86f0-accba0776ed0" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347576 1034 "2" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347576 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535404 true] [17592186347576 1111 #uuid "c3b448b6-88e6-5d8f-9478-834c71b11458" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347577 1017 #edb/ref 17592186347578 13194139535404 true] [17592186347577 1089 "q-75278" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347577 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535404 true] [17592186347577 1100 "A curve is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t-11,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t+5,\\,0\\le t<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nDetermine the values of $t$ at which the normal to the curve is horizontal." 13194139535404 true] [17592186347577 1113 #uuid "e5eafad9-4c2d-5469-bbd9-3cd0fcca968a" 13194139535404 true] [17592186347577 1145 "The normal is horizontal if the tangent is vertical. Therefore, we require ${x}^{′}(t)=0$ while ${y}^{′}(t)\\ne 0.$\n\nSo, we first find the derivatives of $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=12\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t.\\end{aligned}\